<section class="section bg-white"><div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="mb-6">Product Identity</h2><div class="max-w-3xl overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"><table class="w-full text-sm bg-white"><tbody>{specs.map(([k,v],i)=>(<tr class={`border-b border-gray-100 ${i%2===0?'bg-white':'bg-gray-50/50'}`}><td class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary w-1/3">{k}</td><td class="py-3 px-5 text-gray-600">{v}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div></div></section>

<section class="section dot-pattern"><div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="text-center mb-6">Available Configurations</h2><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"><table class="w-full text-sm bg-white"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b-2 border-gray-200"><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Kit</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Content per Vial</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Total IU</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary">Best For</th></tr></thead><tbody>{configs.map((r,i)=>(<tr class={`border-b border-gray-100 ${i%2===0?'bg-white':'bg-gray-50/50'}`}><td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">{r[0]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-accent-dark font-medium text-sm">{r[1]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-accent-dark font-medium">{r[2]}</td><td class="py-3 px-5 text-gray-600 text-sm">{r[3]}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div></div></section>

<section class="section bg-white"><div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="mb-6">Research Background</h2><div class="max-w-4xl"><p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">Human Growth Hormone is a 191-amino acid, single-chain polypeptide synthesized by somatotroph cells in the anterior pituitary. It is the primary regulator of postnatal somatic growth and a key metabolic hormone — controlling the GH/IGF-1 axis via hypothalamic GHRH (+) and somatostatin (-) regulation.</p>
<h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3">Physiological Roles</h3><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 mb-6"><table class="w-full text-sm bg-white"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b-2 border-gray-200"><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">System</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">GH Effect</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Mechanism</th></tr></thead><tbody>{physiology.map((r,i)=>(<tr class={`border-b border-gray-100 ${i%2===0?'bg-white':'bg-gray-50/50'}`}><td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary text-sm">{r[0]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-accent-dark font-medium text-sm">{r[1]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600 text-xs">{r[2]}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div>
<h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3">Research Focus Areas</h3><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-6">{focusAreas.map(([a,f])=>(<div class="card p-4"><span class="font-semibold text-primary text-sm">{a}</span><p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-1">{f}</p></div>))}</div>
<h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3">HGH vs Growth Hormone Secretagogues (GHS)</h3><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"><table class="w-full text-sm bg-white"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b-2 border-gray-200"><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Aspect</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-accent-dark">HGH (Direct)</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">GHS (e.g. CJC-1295)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{hghVsGhs.map((r,i)=>(<tr class={`border-b border-gray-100 ${i%2===0?'bg-white':'bg-gray-50/50'}`}><td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary text-sm">{r[0]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-accent-dark font-medium text-sm">{r[1]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600 text-sm">{r[2]}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div></div></div></section>

<section class="section bg-surface"><div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="text-center mb-6">Quality Specifications</h2><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"><table class="w-full text-sm bg-white"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b-2 border-gray-200"><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Parameter</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary">Method</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary">Criterion</th></tr></thead><tbody>{qcSpecs.map((r,i)=>(<tr class={`border-b border-gray-100 ${i%2===0?'bg-white':'bg-gray-50/50'}`}><td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-primary text-sm">{r[0]}</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600 text-xs">{r[1]}</td><td class="py-3 px-5 text-accent-dark font-medium text-sm">{r[2]}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div><p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-4 text-center">HGH quality analysis combines RP-HPLC, mass spectrometry, and SDS-PAGE — all three applied to ensure research-grade quality for this 22 kDa protein.</p></div></section>

<section class="section bg-white"><div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="text-center mb-6">Tiered Wholesale Pricing</h2><div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm"><table class="w-full text-sm bg-white"><thead><tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b-2 border-gray-200"><th class="text-left py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary">Volume</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary">Discount</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary">For</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pricing.map((r,i)=>(<tr class={`border-b border-gray-100 ${i%2===0?'bg-white':'bg-gray-50/50'}`}><td class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-primary">{r[0]}</td><td class="py-3 px-5 text-accent-dark font-medium">{r[1]}</td><td class="py-3 px-5 text-gray-600 text-sm">{r[2]}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div></div></section>

<section class="section bg-surface"><div class="container-narrow mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="text-center mb-8">FAQ</h2><div class="space-y-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
<details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">What's the difference between HGH and GHS peptides (CJC-1295, Ipamorelin)?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">HGH directly activates GH receptors on target tissues and stimulates IGF-1. GHS peptides (CJC-1295, Ipamorelin) stimulate pituitary release of endogenous GH. For direct GH receptor studies: use HGH. For GH axis regulation studies: use GHS peptides. In body composition research, HGH gives precise dose control; GHS peptides produce more physiological but less controllable responses.</p></details>
<details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">How should HGH be reconstituted and stored?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">Reconstitute with sterile or bacteriostatic water — add diluent gently down vial wall, don't squirt onto powder. Swirl gently (never shake or vortex — denatures protein). Store reconstituted at 2–8°C, use within 7–14 days. Never freeze-thaw — causes aggregation and bioactivity loss.</p></details>
<details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">Which kit size should I order?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">Rodent research: 100 IU kit (10 IU vials) for weight-based dosing. Larger animal models or high-concentration cell culture: 150 IU or 200 IU kits. Uncertain? Start with 100 IU evaluation. <a href="/contact/" class="text-accent-dark hover:underline">Contact us</a> — share your model and we'll recommend the right configuration.</p></details>
<details class="card group cursor-pointer"><summary class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-accent">How do you verify it's actually intact HGH and not a fragment?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-sm">Three methods: (1) Mass spectrometry confirms MW ~22,125 Da ±5 Da — a fragment would show different mass. (2) SDS-PAGE shows single band at ~22 kDa — multiple bands = impurities or degradation. (3) RP-HPLC confirms ≥99% single-peak purity. All three in our QC release testing for research-grade HGH.</p></details>
</div></div></section>

<section class="section bg-white"><div class="container-wide mx-auto px-4"><h2 class="text-center mb-6">Related Products</h2><div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
